<?xml version="1.0"?>
<body language="English">
	<row id="msg_0420_00000" index="0">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Hustler Profiles</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00001" index="1">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Snap</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00002" index="2">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">We ALWAYS watchin’ you!\nIt’s time for Hustler Profiles!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00003" index="3">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">That town, this town,\nbringin’ people together.\nThe Street Corner Channel.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00004" index="4">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This boy LOVE Bug types! He so\nenergetic, and he don’t mind runnin’\nthrough thick grass to catch Bug-type\nhomies! He do what he want, on the\nhills and in the fields, this Bug Catcher!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00005" index="5">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These two always together.\nThey got the same birthday.\nThey always eat together.\nYou think you can tell ’em apart?\nThese Twins!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00006" index="6">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Flyin’ majestic through the sky.\nRejectin’ the land for the open air.\nGracefully flappin’ its wings. Ridin’ the\nwind to soar high in the sky.\nI wanna fly up there too sometime!\nThe Bird Keeper!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00007" index="7">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Singin’ in the cabin.\nLaa... Laa... La la la la...\nThe plan is a three-night, four-\nday trip. To fish off the boat, hike\nin the mountains, and look for EEVEE to\nthe east and west. That’s the Camper!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00008" index="8">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Throwin’ up a peace sign, stuffin’\ndrinks in a cooler, smilin’ big\nwhile hikin’ through the mountains, you\ncan see her clear on the horizon.\nOh no! Forgot the lunchbox! The number\none rule is protect nature.\nThe Picnicker!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00009" index="9">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Accidentally sniffed up some ocean\nwater, now his nose hurt. Swimmin’\naround the rocks, pushin’ ahead with a\nbreaststroke, swimmin’ nonstop,\nand gettin’ a leg cramp! His lungs\nexpand easy but it’s a unlucky day--\nit’s rainin’! That poor Swimmer!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00010" index="10">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A silhouette like Venus. A\nadorably dazzlin’ smile. A nickname of\n“Mermaid.” Swimmin’ around carefree in\nthe early afternoon. Hungry but\non a diet. Mad thirsty\nfans. Drops of water in her dimples.\nPlayin’ in the water instead of takin’\na walk, this Swimmer!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00011" index="11">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Droppin’ a line in the cold water, in\nhopes of catchin’ somethin’ big.\nThe line get yanked. The float drop\nunderwater. What he catch? Some\nlively rubber boots! Poor Fisherman!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00012" index="12">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The day done ended, but it’s still\nbright. That’s weird, you’d think.\nThere’s a crazy fire burnin’, and it\nlook like it’s finna burn ’em.\nHe don’t need a candle. He a human\non fire, carelessly playin’ with fire.\nThe Firebreather!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00013" index="13">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This homie hard, ain’t it?\nThe tail such a great shape.\nWanna trade figurines? Wanna come\nover and see my collection?\nOh ayo! This mark in the wrong place.\nLook like I got finessed with a fake...\nBut it’s art anyway!\nThat’s a Poké Maniac!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00014" index="14">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">I can break ten roof tiles in one chop!\nSome people think I’m just a hooligan.\nThe palm of my hand get covered\nin blisters. I never forget to bow, and\nI yell to hype myself up!\nI’m the Black Belt!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00015" index="15">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Hold it close, cheek to cheek. I always\nwanna be with you, surrounded by\nwonderful homies. I’ll mumble your\nname. So happy, I’m dizzy.\nI LOVE homies! That’s a Pokéfan!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00016" index="16">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A strong guy on a boat, plowin’\nthrough the waves. Dancin’ and singin’\nand havin’ a good ol’ time. But gentle\nas kittens once they back on land.\nThat’s a Sailor!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00017" index="17">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Had mad success. Learnin’ from\ndoin’ it over and over. Carryin’\nnotebooks everywhere. Goin’ to classes\nfor gifted kids.\nA wonderful Hustler, that\nSchool Kid!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00018" index="18">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ayo kid, outta my way! If you hang\naround, I’mma smack you! Move\noutta the way. Outta the way. My Bike\ncomin’ through! It’s SO loud, you’ll\ncover your ears! We line up and block\nthe road. Try to stop us Bikers!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0420_00019" index="19">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Yaho... Yaho... Yahohoho...\nSingin’ loud without worryin’\nabout who around. A bearded man\nyellin’ at the sky. From the far\nmountain. Yahohoho... So happy the\necho came back to the Hiker!</language>
	</row>
</body>
